From 4da1c814d2cc94fc0b20b53a613cdb27469b1e43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:43:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] asahi: keep the tile under fully masked draws on the M5
 Pro

On the M5 Pro (G17S), as on G17P, a covered fragment with no tile store
still dirties the tile, which then stores undefined colour at the end of
the tile. A draw with every colour channel masked off (a stencil-only
pass over a cleared RGBA8 target) left (0,0,0,0) where the clear had
been; the following blended draw then read a destination alpha of zero.
Measured on the machine: clear to (0,0,0,1), draw with
glColorMask(0,0,0,0), read back 00000000 instead of ff000000. Blending,
partial colour masks and destination-alpha reads are correct.

The epilog already has G17P's answer: preserve_zero_mask keeps the
destination with a tile load/store pair when the write mask is empty
(and for attachments the shader never writes). Turn it on for the
Gallium epilog on G17S and G17C, the same M5 core. G17G keeps its
validated behaviour; the Vulkan driver's epilog policy is unchanged.

After this the probe reads ff000000 and the GLES smoke test's
stencil-then-blend scene reads bf808080, as zink does.

Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM Claude
---
 src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c b/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c
index 4c91c155988..2653aea86e2 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/asahi/agx_state.c
@@ -3798,6 +3798,14 @@ agx_update_fs(struct agx_batch *batch)
                               : 0,
    };
    agx_fs_epilog_apply_device_policy(dev->chip, &link_key.epilog.fs);
+   /* G17S (and G17C, the same core) share G17P's tile behaviour: a covered
+    * fragment with no tile store still dirties the tile, which then stores
+    * undefined colour at EOT. Measured on the M5 Pro: a draw with every
+    * colour channel masked off left (0,0,0,0) where the clear had been. Keep
+    * the destination with a load/store pair, as G17P does. G17G is left as
+    * its validated line has it. */
+   if (agx_chip_g17_m5(dev->chip) && dev->chip != AGX_CHIP_G17G)
+      link_key.epilog.fs.preserve_zero_mask = true;
 
    for (unsigned i = 0; i < PIPE_MAX_COLOR_BUFS; ++i) {
       link_key.epilog.fs.rt_formats[i] = batch->key.cbufs[i].format;
